OL,3,GNEWSACouncil plan for tech to beat big
OL,4,Afreeze on roads
OL,5,
OL,6,FBradford Council could stop
OL,7,Fautomatically gritting its whole A-road
OL,8,Fnetwork whenever freezing weather is
OL,9,Fforecast.
OL,11,FA new report from the authority said it
OL,12,Fwanted to move away from an "all out"
OL,13,Fapproach and instead use hi-tech road
OL,14,Ftemperature sensors, thermal mapping
OL,15,Fand detailed weather forecasts to treat
OL,16,Fareas most at risk of ice.
OL,18,FThe authority currently grits 819 miles
OL,19,F(1318km) of "Priority 1" roads,
OL,20,Fcovering major routes serving places
OL,21,Fsuch as hospitals, schools and town
OL,22,Fcentres, ahead of any severe cold snap.
OL,23,APub: 04-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,382,380,200,160,0,100
